# Project: Countries Catalog

University educational project. A catalog web app built with React that lets users
search countries, sort results, and open a country details page.
Data source: REST Countries API v5 (https://api.restcountries.com/countries/v5),
Bearer auth via `VITE_API_KEY`.

## Stack (do not substitute without asking)
- Vite + React + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Redux Toolkit (createSlice, createAsyncThunk) + react-redux
- React Router (data fetching goes through Redux, not through router loaders)
- styled-components for styling (no CSS modules, no UI kits)
- Unit tests: Jest + React Testing Library (+ @testing-library/jest-dom, user-event)
- E2E tests: Cypress
- ESLint + Prettier

## UI (from the assignment's design, adapted to countries)
Two pages, English interface.
1. Search page: header with logo, title, text input, "Search by" toggle (Name / Region),
   Search button. Below: results bar ("N countries found") and "Sort by" toggle
   (Population / Area). Then a grid of country cards (flag, name, population, region).
   Footer with logo.
2. Country page: header with logo, big flag, name, region + subregion, capital, population,
   area, languages, currencies. Below: "More countries in the same region" (grid of cards).
   Footer.

## Architecture rules
- 100% decomposition: every visual block is its own component. No component renders
  more than one logical block of UI. Prefer small components.
- Smart/dumb split:
  - dumb (presentational) components live in `src/components/`; they get data and
    callbacks via props only, never touch Redux, router hooks, or fetch.
  - smart (container) components live in `src/containers/`; they connect to Redux
    (useAppSelector / useAppDispatch) and router hooks, and pass props to dumb components.
  - pages live in `src/pages/` and only compose containers.
- Wrap the app in an `ErrorBoundary` class component (src/components/ErrorBoundary) that
  catches render errors and shows a friendly fallback. Add a render-error test for it.
- Folder layout:
  src/
    api/            REST Countries client + response types
    app/            store.ts, typed hooks, router setup
    features/countries/   slice, thunks (actions), selectors, types
    components/     dumb components (each in its own folder with test + styles)
    containers/     smart components
    pages/
    styles/         theme, global styles
    utils/
    test/           test utils, mocks, setupTests
- Data fetching only inside Redux async thunks (actions). Components never call fetch directly.
- Sorting is done client-side in memoized selectors (the API has no sorting).
- Typed everything: no `any`; API responses have explicit TypeScript interfaces.
- Named exports for components, one component per file, file name = component name.

## REST Countries API notes (v5, verified)
- Base URL: `https://api.restcountries.com/countries/v5`
- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <key>` (from `VITE_API_KEY` in `.env.local`; never commit/log the key)
- Envelope: `{ data: { objects: T[], meta: { total, count, limit, offset, more, request_id?, duration? } } }`
- List: `GET /?q=` (full-text, case-insensitive, many fields) or `GET /?region=` (case-insensitive;
  known values: Africa, Americas, Antarctic, Asia, Europe, Oceania). Empty results → 200 + `objects: []`
- Read: `GET /codes.alpha_3/{CODE}` → `objects` length 0 or 1 (unknown code → empty list, not 404)
- Field paths: `names.common`, `codes.alpha_3`, `flag.url_png` / `flag.url_svg` / `flag.description`,
  `region`, `subregion`, `capitals[].name`, `population`, `area.kilometers`, `languages[]`, `currencies[]`
- Pagination: default `limit` 25; free plan max 100/request; follow `offset` while `meta.more`.
  `response_fields` works on list and read. No usable server-side sort — sort client-side.
- Errors: 401 `authKeyNotFound`/`authKeyMissing`; 400 `limitOutOfRange`; 403 `limitPaidPlanOnly` /
  `originNotAllowed`; map 429 → rate limited. Error body: `{ errors: [{ message, code }] }`
- CORS: browser Origin `http://localhost:5173` is rejected (`originNotAllowed`) for keys without that
  origin allowlisted. Local/preview use Vite proxy at `/api/countries/v5` that strips Origin and
  injects Authorization. `.env.development` / `.env.production` set `VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/countries/v5`.

## Routing
- `/` : empty state, "0 countries found", no request is made.
- `/search/:query` : new search redirects here (URL-encoded query). Opening this URL
  directly must run the search and show results.
- `/country/:code` : country details page (cca3 code); clicking a card navigates here.
- `*` : 404 page; invalid URLs redirect/render here.
- Switching search type (Name/Region) or sort type must NOT change the route.
- Search type defaults to Name when the page is opened directly via URL.

## Environments
- `.env.development` and `.env.production` with `VITE_` variables; commit `.env.example` only,
  never real secrets. Dev server for development; optimized production build
  (`npm run build`, `npm run preview`).

## Testing
- Coverage target: > 60% overall (aim higher), measured with Jest coverage (`npm run test:coverage`).
- Use snapshot tests for dumb components.
- Unit tests for slice reducers, thunks (mock fetch), and selectors.
- At least 5 Cypress e2e tests (search, sort, open details, 404, direct URL to /search/:query).
- Tests live next to the code (`Component.test.tsx`).

## Git workflow
- GitFlow: `main`, `develop`, `feature/task-N-short-name`. Never commit to `main` directly.
- Conventional commits (feat:, fix:, test:, chore:, refactor:, docs:).

## Working style
- Work on one assignment task at a time; do not implement later tasks early.
- After each task: the app builds, lint passes, tests pass.
- If something is unclear or data is missing, ask instead of inventing it.
- Keep a short README section describing how to run, test, and build.
